**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.log
**/coverage
.git
.github
.vscode
.idea
# The frontend image (frontend/Dockerfile) needs the full frontend workspace
# source — index.html, src, config — to run `vite build`. The backend/worker
# images only ever COPY frontend/package.json, so keeping the rest in context
# doesn't bloat their builds (it's just not COPYed). The blanket `**/node_modules`
# and `**/dist` rules above already strip the heavy frontend artifacts.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
infra
# Local-only dev backdoor — must NEVER enter an image build context, even from a
# dirty worktree. `devAuth.ts` mints a full session with no auth (bypassing the
# OWNER_GITHUB_ID gate) and is guarded only by NODE_ENV; excluding the source
# here is defense-in-depth so a baked image can't ship the backdoor at all.
backend/src/routes/devAuth.ts
backend/scripts/seed-dev.mjs
*.png
PLAN.md
SPEC.md
README.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
docker-compose.yml
